\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou art coming, O my Saviour,
\par Thou art coming, O my King,
\par In Thy beauty, all-resplendent,
\par In Thy glory all-transcendent ;
\par Well may we rejoice and sing ;
\par Coming ! In the opening east
\par Herald brightness slowly swells ;
\par Coming ! O my glorious Priest,
\par Hear we not Thy golden bells ?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou art coming, Thou art coming ;
\par We shall meet Thee on Thy way,
\par We shall see Thee, we shall know Thee,
\par We shall bless Thee, we shall show Thee
\par All our hearts could never say ;
\par What an anthem that will be,
\par Ringing out our love to Thee,
\par Pouring out our rapture sweet,
\par At Thine own all-glorious feet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O the joy to see Thee reigning,
\par Thee, our own beloved Lord !
\par Every tongue Thy name confessing,
\par Worship, honour, glory, blessing
\par Brought to Thee with one accord ;
\par Thee, our Master and our Friend,
\par Vindicated and enthroned,
\par Unto earth's remotest end
\par Glorified, adored, and owned ! 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

